# Phase 18 assignment stable HashSet bucket parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-24 15:14:17 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Code revision: `cc49b573`
- Host: macOS AArch64, Rust 1.85.0
- Java reference: pinned offline Maven build

## Change

- Protocol JSON decoding now models Java `HashSet` equality checks within
  stable `MessageQueueAssignment` hash buckets. Same-mode assignments with
  equal queue and attachment-map hashes deduplicate even when their attachment
  maps differ (the `Aa`/`BB` Java String-hash collision); duplicate null-queue
  rows with matching hashes retain Java's `NullPointerException` behavior.
- `MessageQueueAssignment` keeps lawful all-fields Rust `Eq`/`Hash`; the
  decoder uses a separate Java bucket index. The Java lookup fixture adds the
  stable collision, different-hash control, and null-queue cases. It also marks
  the existing different-mode collision as `sameMode: false`.
- The response input corpus now has 33 Set-field cases plus seven root-shape
  cases. Source commit: `cc49b573 fix(protocol): match stable assignment set buckets`.

